    "statement": "Subject: Framed delivery records for segmented text\n\nText arrives in source segments and is transmitted in byte-limited chunks. Each nonempty chunk also adds a framing header, so the transmission budget depends on where chunk boundaries occur.\n\nThe text consists of Unicode scalar values. Under UTF-8, a value uses 1 byte for U+0000..U+007F, 2 for U+0080..U+07FF, 3 for U+0800..U+FFFF, and 4 otherwise. Surrogates are invalid.\n\nFor each request, start a new transmission with no open chunk and process a consecutive character range from left to right:\n\n* A chunk contains at most `C` UTF-8 payload bytes and never splits a character.\n* A chunk cannot cross a source-segment boundary. Reaching that boundary closes it.\n* Every nonempty chunk contributes exactly `H` additional wire bytes for its header. Headers do not count toward `C`.\n* The request budget `B` limits total wire bytes: payload bytes plus headers.\n* Before sending a character, include its payload width and, if it would begin a new chunk, one header. If this would exceed `B`, stop before that character. A header is never sent without at least one character.\n* Completing the requested range has cause `END`; every earlier stop has ",
